{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2161-03-17 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I understand you've been having trouble breathing lately. Can you tell me more about what’s been going on?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2161-03-17 11:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, it feels like I'm breathing through a straw. It's been getting worse over the past two weeks."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2161-03-17 11:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. And have you noticed any changes in your secretions from the trach?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2161-03-17 11:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, they used to be clear and thin, but now they’re thick and green."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2161-03-17 11:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That could be a sign of infection. You mentioned dizziness too—when does that happen?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2161-03-17 11:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yesterday, I felt like the room was spinning. I almost fell when I stood up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2161-03-17 11:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll check your blood pressure when you stand to see if it drops. That could explain the dizziness."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2161-03-17 11:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. I also get sharp pain on my sides when I take deep breaths."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2161-03-17 11:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s called pleuritic chest pain. We’ll get a CT scan to make sure there’s no clot or pneumonia."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2161-03-17 11:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve been on cipro and prednisone for five days. I don’t feel any better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2161-03-17 11:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Sometimes with your airway history, secretions build up and block airflow. The meds might not reach deep enough."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2161-03-17 11:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So what’s the plan?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2161-03-17 11:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll start with IV fluids for dehydration and dizziness. We’ll also do a chest CT and consider a bronchoscopy."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2161-03-17 11:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Bronchoscopy? Is that safe with my trach?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2161-03-17 11:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we can go through your trach. It will help us see if there’s a blockage and clean it out if needed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2161-03-17 14:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your chest X-ray didn’t show pneumonia, but your white blood cell count is rising, which suggests infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2161-03-17 14:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "But the X-ray is normal?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2161-03-17 14:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, but sometimes infections don’t show up right away. We’re still concerned and want to rule out a clot."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2161-03-18 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. We’re scheduling your bronchoscopy for today. It should help clear the secretions."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2161-03-18 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Will it hurt?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2161-03-18 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll be sedated, so you won’t feel it. Afterward, you might feel a little sore, but it’s usually well tolerated."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2161-03-18 13:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The bronchoscopy went well. They found your airway was patent but had some thick secretions. They cleared them out."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2161-03-18 13:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So that was the problem?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2161-03-18 13:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Likely a big part of it. Your breathing should improve now that the blockage is gone."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2161-03-18 13:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I still feel a bit dizzy when I stand."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2161-03-18 13:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your blood pressure drops when you stand—orthostatic hypotension. We’re giving IV fluids and encouraging you to drink more."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2161-03-19 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We did a CT scan last night. It shows some hazy spots in your lungs, which could be from infection or inflammation."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2161-03-19 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is it pneumonia?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2161-03-19 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s hard to say for sure. The spots are patchy. But there’s no pulmonary embolus, which is good news."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2161-03-19 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about the dizziness?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2161-03-19 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your blood pressure is stabilizing with fluids. We’ll keep monitoring it."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2161-03-19 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my breathing?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2161-03-19 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re on room air and your oxygen is stable. The bronchoscopy helped. We’re continuing with nebulizers."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2161-03-19 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your sputum culture came back—just normal mouth bacteria, no infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2161-03-19 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So no antibiotics?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2161-03-19 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll stop cipro. The green secretions were likely from inflammation, not infection."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2161-03-20 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Your white count is coming down, which means your body is calming down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2161-03-20 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel less short of breath."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2161-03-20 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Great. We’re also adjusting your asthma meds. You were getting too much albuterol, which made your heart race."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2161-03-20 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I did feel my heart racing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2161-03-20 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We switched to Xopenex, which is gentler. Your heart rate is normal now."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2161-03-21 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. We’re planning to discharge you tomorrow if things stay stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2161-03-21 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What about the spots on my lungs?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2161-03-21 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "They’re likely from the inflammation and resolving now. No need for further action unless symptoms return."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2161-03-21 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "And my throat issues?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2161-03-21 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The bronchoscopy showed laryngeal stenosis. We’ve scheduled an ENT follow-up to discuss options."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2161-03-21 10:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. And my GERD?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2161-03-21 10:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We increased your omeprazole to twice daily to reduce aspiration risk, given your airway issues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2161-03-22 09:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re ready to go home today. Your breathing is stable, dizziness is gone, and labs are normal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2161-03-22 09:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "What should I watch for?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2161-03-22 09:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "If you have trouble breathing, fever, or dizziness again, come back. Otherwise, keep up with trach care and see ENT."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2161-03-22 09:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll do that. Thank you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2161-03-22 09:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. We’ll send all your discharge instructions and meds with you."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2161-03-22 09:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is the thyroid nodule from the CT serious?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2161-03-22 09:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "It’s small and likely not related. But we recommend a thyroid ultrasound as a precaution."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2161-03-22 09:07:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I’ll follow up on that too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2161-03-22 09:08:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good plan. Take care, and call if anything changes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2161-03-22 09:09:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. Thanks again."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2161-03-22 09:10:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing great. Keep up the good work with your breathing treatments."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2161-03-22 09:11:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. I feel so much better already."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 61,
      "time": "2161-03-22 09:12:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s wonderful to hear. We’re glad we could help."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 62,
      "time": "2161-03-22 09:13:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Can I travel soon?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 63,
      "time": "2161-03-22 09:14:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Wait a few days. Make sure you’re stable. Bring your nebulizer if you fly."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 64,
      "time": "2161-03-22 09:15:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. Thanks for all the advice."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 65,
      "time": "2161-03-22 09:16:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take it easy and rest."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 66,
      "time": "2161-03-22 09:17:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I will. See you at follow-up."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 67,
      "time": "2161-03-22 09:18:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, and call anytime if you need us."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2161-03-17 10:42:00",
    "admission_end": "2161-03-22 14:55:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A 31-year-old woman with a history of tracheobronchomalacia, chronic tracheostomy, asthma, and GERD was admitted for worsening shortness of breath, thick green tracheal secretions, and dizziness. She had been on ciprofloxacin and prednisone without improvement. Evaluation revealed leukocytosis and orthostatic hypotension. A bronchoscopy cleared obstructive secretions, leading to symptom improvement. A chest CT showed ground-glass opacities concerning for infection, though sputum cultures were negative, suggesting resolving inflammation. Her tachycardia was linked to albuterol use and resolved with medication adjustment. Dizziness resolved with IV fluid rehydration. The omeprazole dose was increased for GERD prophylaxis. She was discharged home in stable condition with follow-up arranged for laryngeal stenosis and a thyroid nodule noted on imaging.",
    "problems": [
      "Other diseases of trachea and bronchus",
      "Asthma, unspecified type, with (acute) exacerbation",
      "Esophageal reflux",
      "Orthostatic hypotension",
      "Tracheostomy status",
      "Stenosis of larynx",
      "Dehydration",
      "Unspecified chronic bronchitis"
    ]
  }
}
